From 5a42e7e071c3434d8f9e05454d848d14c950e81a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kryxzort <101042137+Kryxzort@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 18:21:46 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 109/128] render: a colour-blend layer takes its colour and
 alpha once
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A layer with a colour blend mode (≠ 0, ≠ 31) is a flag-0x10 layer in WE too (GH 0x140212f90).
Its base and effects draw with the context colour (1, 1, 1, 1), and the layer's colour and
alpha are set for the BLENDMODE draw alone (GH 0x140214b50, 0x1402321d0). LWE bound the layer's
g_Color4 to both the base pass and the genericimage3 BLENDMODE pass, so a 0.3 layer came out at
0.09, and a colour of 0.5 at 0.25. Its base pass now reads (1, 1, 1, 1), as the fogged layers'
does (0107).

Measured on the 12 library scenes with such a layer whose alpha or colour isn't 1:
2371103399 0.071 → 0.013 against WE (its two mode-7 layers at alpha 0.3: 128 → 143.6 where
they differ, WE 142.9), 3309103316 0.141 → 0.136 (64.3 there, WE 64.5). The other 10 are
unchanged within the clock digits' noise.

Origin: ours
Why: docs/player/spikes/we-lwe-gap-audit.md "3D scenes against WE" (2371103399, 3309103316)
Status: candidate-for-upstream
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Vg3T4kWN88ooeafgoHLbfM
---
 src/core/WallpaperEngine/Render/Objects/CImage.cpp | 8 +++++---
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/core/WallpaperEngine/Render/Objects/CImage.cpp b/src/core/WallpaperEngine/Render/Objects/CImage.cpp
index 3a9c014..a54e974 100644
--- a/src/core/WallpaperEngine/Render/Objects/CImage.cpp
+++ b/src/core/WallpaperEngine/Render/Objects/CImage.cpp
@@ -1255,7 +1255,8 @@ void CImage::setup () {
     // (genericimage2/3); the renderer then adds FOG_DIST / FOG_HEIGHT to a draw whose FOG combo is on, from the scene's
     // fog. 3477054430's moon, 180 units out with fog from 6.5 to 500, is 12 % darker that way in WE. Ours: only the
     // layers that end up fogged (world-placed, material FOG on) take the extra pass; the blend-mode-only one stays
-    // genericimage3's (no library scene with fog has a layer whose material turns FOG off)
+    // genericimage3's (no library scene with fog has a layer whose material turns FOG off). Either way the base pass
+    // draws with the colour (1, 1, 1, 1), below
     const int colorBlendMode = this->m_image.colorBlendMode->value->getInt ();
     const bool blendPass = colorBlendMode > 0 && colorBlendMode != 31;
     const auto& fog = this->getScene ().getScene ().fog;
@@ -1305,8 +1306,9 @@ void CImage::setup () {
 
 	// WE draws a flag-0x10 layer's base and effects with the context colour (1, 1, 1, 1) and sets the layer's colour
 	// and alpha (GH 0x1402321d0) for this last draw only (GH 0x140214b50), so they apply once. 3276522107's lit train
-	// (alpha keyframed 0 … 0.3 … 1) flickers as in WE that way; with both draws taking them its 0.3 frames were 0.09
-	if (fogPass && !this->m_hasPuppetMesh) {
+	// (alpha keyframed 0 … 0.3 … 1) flickers as in WE that way; with both draws taking them its 0.3 frames were 0.09.
+	// The same for a colour blend mode's draw: 2371103399's two blend-mode-7 layers at alpha 0.3 came out at 128 where WE has 143
+	if (!this->m_hasPuppetMesh) {
 	    this->m_passes.front ()->addUniform ("g_Color4", &UNIT_COLOR4);
 	}
 
